{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources","id":1100981,"title":"Management and Human Resources","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-06T15:21:04-07:00","id":1100981,"title":"Management and Human Resources","content":"I'm thoroughly confused by the sidebar on 595 of M20. I can't see a difference between a technocrat who uses mind 3/ correspondence 3 to summon a helicopter and a normal human who does the exact same thing. Both need the Resources and Retainers ,(or appropriate underling providing background), both have to make a phone call and wait. If you have the backgrounds it seems having sphere magic is a straight downgrade, as you have to roll the effect. Is there any explanation for this or is it like &quot;chi powers&quot; in HDYDT? (A straight downgrade based on the paradigm chosen.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/544-deadpoint","name":"Deadpoint","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T15:41:07-07:00","id":1100989,"title":"","content":"It's another example of the straight downgrade magic received in M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T16:03:52-07:00","id":1101000,"title":"","content":"I suppose it could be justified if the helicopter wouldn't normally be under the mage's control. You're arranging things in order to rapidly induce the pilot to come, regardless of what they're supposed to be doing. Making them an offer they can't refuse, and the magick sort of expedites the process of convincing them (otherwise, you'd need to do a bunch of roleplaying).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T16:42:51-07:00","id":1101020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadpoint</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources#post1100981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thoroughly confused by the sidebar on 595 of M20. I can't see a difference between a technocrat who uses mind 3/ correspondence 3 to summon a helicopter and a normal human who does the exact same thing. Both need the Resources and Retainers ,(or appropriate underling providing background), both have to make a phone call and wait. If you have the backgrounds it seems having sphere magic is a straight downgrade, as you have to roll the effect. Is there any explanation for this or is it like &quot;chi powers&quot; in HDYDT? (A straight downgrade based on the paradigm chosen.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is that 100% of the time, the helicopter will succeed in coming and be exactly the kind they want. The point of the Technocracy is they've degraded their magic to the point virtually anyone can do what they want but they will do it BETTER.<br /> <br /> For example, you may have to spend 60 million dollars building a skyscrapper with Matter 5/Prime 2 to build it in a couple of weeks coincidentally.<br /> <br /> But it WILL be built.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-06-2017, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T17:21:01-07:00","id":1101032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources?p=1101020#post1101020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The answer is that 100% of the time, the helicopter will succeed in coming and be exactly the kind they want. The point of the Technocracy is they've degraded their magic to the point virtually anyone can do what they want but they will do it BETTER.<br /> <br /> For example, you may have to spend 60 million dollars building a Skyscrapper with Matter 5/Prime 2 to build it in a couple of weeks coincidentally.<br /> <br /> But it WILL be built.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't an M20 thing, either. In Mage: The Sorcerer's Crusade, many of the powers available to members of the Order of Reason are, by design, basically more effective mundane feats. It's all a part of their commitment to the &quot;Casual Rule&quot;, that members didn't get to violate until they reached Arete 4+.<br /> <br /> On the plus side, it gave us a number of different ways to look at the Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T17:31:17-07:00","id":1101036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources?p=1101032#post1101032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't an M20 thing, either. In Mage: The Sorcerer's Crusade, many of the powers available to members of the Order of Reason are, by design, basically more effective mundane feats. It's all a part of their commitment to the &quot;Casual Rule&quot;, that members didn't get to violate until they reached Arete 4+.<br /> <br /> On the plus side, it gave us a number of different ways to look at the Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also makes it so the Technocracy does have a disadvantage to the Traditions because they have the Illuminati's power over society. It's only a problem if you think the Technocracy should be able to do what the Traditions do, which is what they're explicitly not about.<br /> <br /> And if you're wondering what the difference is between knocking around a guy with &quot;Enhanced Interrogation&quot; and getting him to fess up with Mind 3 is.<br /> <br /> Well, Mind 3 works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T01:31:16-07:00","id":1101148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadpoint</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources#post1100981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thoroughly confused by the sidebar on 595 of M20. I can't see a difference between a technocrat who uses mind 3/ correspondence 3 to summon a helicopter and a normal human who does the exact same thing. Both need the Resources and Retainers ,(or appropriate underling providing background), both have to make a phone call and wait. If you have the backgrounds it seems having sphere magic is a straight downgrade, as you have to roll the effect. Is there any explanation for this or is it like &quot;chi powers&quot; in HDYDT? (A straight downgrade based on the paradigm chosen.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It shouldn't be Correspondence I'd say - just Mind if the pilot needs some convincing or courage boost. I think it's also a downgrade as Correspondence 3 because other Mages could Unweave your flight, perhaps. Even if we consider helicopters as a Magickal vehicle, then I'd say that the Correspondence use would be on part of the pilot, not the Technocrat summoning a helicopter. But helicopters are not Magickal anymore (unless they are in a particular case, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-07-2017, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T05:49:49-07:00","id":1101185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources?p=1101148#post1101148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It shouldn't be Correspondence I'd say - just Mind if the pilot needs some convincing or courage boost. I think it's also a downgrade as Correspondence 3 because other Mages could Unweave your flight, perhaps. Even if we consider helicopters as a Magickal vehicle, then I'd say that the Correspondence use would be on part of the pilot, not the Technocrat summoning a helicopter. But helicopters are not Magickal anymore (unless they are in a particular case, of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>You need Correspondence (and moreover at a level equal to Mind) because you're using the Effect over a distance. If the pilot was present with the helicopter, you wouldn't need to summon it.<br /> <br /> If you were using the helicopter as an Instrument for a Correspondence 3 effect, that's another thing entirely...as well as something with precedent in MtAs. As I said in a previous post, the Order of Reason often used their Enlightened Science to expedite otherwise mundane travel. Infiltrators entered buildings using climbing shoes, lockpicks, and grappling hooks. And explorers would use maps and their knowledge of the environment to make over-land journeys much faster, which often involved taking &quot;shortcuts&quot; that covered more distance than should be realistic. It's entirely possible that modern Technocrats only further refined their methods in this regard.<br /> <br /> No, this isn't exactly teleporting (except when it is). But the Order of Reason book made me consider that Correspondence 3 isn't explicitly about &quot;Teleportation&quot;, but rather &quot;Making intervening space and obstacles not a factor in one's movement&quot;. (Which, really, would also justify using Correspondence 3 to walk through walls. It's not like there's an appreciable practical difference between walking through a wall and teleporting to the other side). But I digress.<br /> <br /> Yes, this is all less efficient than just teleporting. But that deliberate limitation is taken in trade-off for something potentially far more important: being Coincidental. There are ways to make teleportation coincidental, yes, but these ways are not always feasible, nor does a character always believe it can be done (or that the character themselves can do it, even if they believe it theoretically possible). Syndicate reps don't usually study the mind-bending physics needed to fold space, nor can they always afford to rely on gear provided by other Conventions. Nor, again, can they afford to employ such Vulgar methods all the time. For everyday purposes, they are more inclined to leverage their connections, interpersonal skills, and knowledge of geography to call in a helicopter, and then make that helicopter transport them to their location faster than it normally could. An Effect that's completely Coincidental, and which wouldn't cause them to fall from the sky if someone used Countermagic on them (like you said, the helicopter itself is established in the Consensus; the Enlightened Management is just there to make it go faster).<br /> <br /> I find that, when it comes to Paradigm-generated limitations, one must remember that these are features of the Sphere system, not bugs. The Sphere descriptions tell us the upper limit of a mage's capabilities at any given level. It's the Focus - Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments - that tells us how much of that a particular mage can use. Whether &quot;Can Use&quot; is determined by what they believe possible, what they are equipped to pull off, or what they dare do in light of Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T01:24:52-07:00","id":1101527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadpoint</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources#post1100981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thoroughly confused by the sidebar on 595 of M20. I can't see a difference between a technocrat who uses mind 3/ correspondence 3 to summon a helicopter and a normal human who does the exact same thing. Both need the Resources and Retainers ,(or appropriate underling providing background), both have to make a phone call and wait. If you have the backgrounds it seems having sphere magic is a straight downgrade, as you have to roll the effect. Is there any explanation for this or is it like &quot;chi powers&quot; in HDYDT? (A straight downgrade based on the paradigm chosen.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a disconnect between the play modes of M20 and MRev, where the Syndicate &quot;management and HR&quot; stuff emerges from. MRev allows props to exist in the unrealized narrative zone, and M20's axis of coincidence decidedly doesn't.<br /> <br /> That said, I expect the intent of Mind3/Corr3 in the example in that sidebar is that the mage is influencing the minds of judges, and is leveraging their backgrounds to do so.<br /> <br /> I think it's an unnecessary complication to the instrument, but I must admit I'd be hard-pressed to name a single thing I think M20 got right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T10:53:05-07:00","id":1101680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources?p=1101527#post1101527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's an unnecessary complication to the instrument...</div> </div> </div> </div>But you can say that about a lot of Instruments in Mage. The tools that mages use to do their magick depend on their beliefs, not on what's simple or easy. A Syndicate rep happens to believe that power comes from resources and connections, that can be leveraged to accomplish far-reaching effects. That's entirely appropriate to their Focus.<br /> <br /> Or is High Ritual Magick any less appropriate, despite often being more complicated than the above? Hours spent drawing intricate circles, making mind-bending numerological calculations, making sure the rite is performed with the correct celestial alignments, collecting rarefied material components, chanting for yet more hours, etc. By contrast, the Syndicate rep just pulls out their cell phone, calls a judge, and makes a deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T12:00:14-07:00","id":1101701,"title":"","content":"Enh. I honestly, find that response not particularly germane to what I was talking about.<br /> <br /> I am not saying that it makes the instrument too inconvenient for <i>the mage</i> so much as it adds overhead to the <i>player</i>. I am saying that it introduces an unneeded layer of prescripting, one not present in the SyndRev, and one that SyndRev did not (to my mind, at least) suffer for lacking.It requires users of HR&amp;M to instantiate into the fictional world in much more definite terms the elements of their paradigm, not as a check on &quot;power&quot; (because there is almost no consideration for &quot;balance&quot; between instruments, as your own example displays) but as a method of preserving M20's axis of coincidence.<br /> <br /> In SyndRev, it is possible for a Matter-using syndic's player to, as part of the terms of their effect, state that a given automobile has an untapped hidden feature that improves its gas mileage. This does not require that the player first establish with the ST that the car is of such-and-such a make, and to have a Background to represent their influence in the manufacturer's factories. Rather, the conspiratorial nature of the world exists in an unrealized state, one that resolves into definite effects at player input. M20's concern about PBD seems to mean that it doesn't have such an unrealized state: we have to know if the feature &quot;really exists&quot;<i> - </i>which meansthe conspiracy has to really exist<i> - </i>because PBD won't permit us to elide these steps, any more than it will allow us to &quot;conjure&quot; a cab<i>.</i><br /> <br /> We know that the WoD is haunted by conspiracies as much as it is haunted by the High Ritualist's choirs of angels - but M20 only requires one of these players to buy Backgrounds to make their host of specters &quot;real.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T08:46:36-07:00","id":1102276,"title":"","content":"I agree with Bluecho, this is a feature not a bug. And it doesn't matter if adds overhead to the player, as, in essence, that's exactly what Practice and Instruments DO. They make the game less one of players (particularly bad players), just handwave away the magic and just say &quot;I use Correspondence 3 to get there.&quot; <br /> <br /> Should Syndicate members be teleporting? Does that make sense for them? Can they touch a pile of leaves and turn it into money? Which leads to my digression, which isn't about the different ways that Correspondence can be used to walk through walls, exccept that it is, because there is still something over and above Focus that used to be called &quot;paradigm&quot; but has been lost in M20 - that iconic thing that held together one Sect and differentiated it from another. Meaning some mages can use Correspodence 3teleport from one side of the wall to the other, some mages can walk through the wall and some mages do other things entirely - like arrange to have someone get through the wall for them or have whatever they want to have happen on the other side of the wall get done by proxy. Some groups may be able to use more than one way. Some groups cannot use some of the ways Some ways to handle the situation require adding in other Spheres, but adding in those other Spheres does increase the functionality of what they are able to accomplish. <br /> <br /> Sure, Intstruments can also be Backgrounds. A Syndicate mage might have Money as an Instrument and have multiple dots in Resources But that adds to what can be accomplished and leads to several different ways to accomplish it. When the Resources are used without magic, there's no chance of a Paradox blowout but there are definitely some issues that can be cleared away by using the Spheres with the Instrument of Money (or finances or whatever). E.g. when the mage uses Resources alone, it's the same as hiring a helicopter pilot like a normal rich person would. Unless they are really rich and have thought ahead to have one standing by, it's going to take finagling, which takes time. When a Syndicate mage uses Spheres and the Instrument-Money, perhaps he is connecting to the underlying hegemony that Syndicate holds over all capitalistic systems. Maybe the Syndicate has a way to co-opt helicopters (or taxis) that are getting ready to go or are ready, but sitting idle. So there's someone who thought they were going to use that helicopter but they just got booted. (Which seems like it makes sense... The helicopter pilot or company gets a deal that can't refuse and boom, here comes your helicopter, Mr. Anderson....<br /> <br /> In some ways I don't see a problem with the character getting really creative and saying things like &quot;The Syndicate has arranged for all cars to have X installed as a secret feature and I am activating it&quot;. So long as X is a coincidental effect that makes sense within the parameters of what cars can do on pretty much every level. In fact, I think that's GREAT, as it can be used again and again in so many ways. It even can illustrate how the Conventions are working together routinely (which is something that gets short shrift... pretty much the game seems to indicate they all hate and despise and undercut each other). To get such a feature installed on all cars, it would take integrating it into the production process in a way that wouldn't tweak the Masses, which implicates Iteration-X (for the technical specs), N.W.O. (because legally requiring something more mundance, like emission control, allows for a system can piggy back onto makes a ton of sense and expedites things) and the Syndicate (for their control of the production process as a whole). Meaning, members of any of those three Conventions could know about and be able to access that feature (depesning on possessing the relevant Spheres and Instruments). The coolness factor of the Technocracy as a whole just went up a notch due to player creativity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T10:51:08-07:00","id":1102299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources?p=1101701#post1101701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enh. I honestly, find that response not particularly germane to what I was talking about.<br /> <br /> I am not saying that it makes the instrument too inconvenient for <i>the mage</i> so much as it adds overhead to the <i>player</i>. I am saying that it introduces an unneeded layer of prescripting, one not present in the SyndRev, and one that SyndRev did not (to my mind, at least) suffer for lacking.It requires users of HR&amp;M to instantiate into the fictional world in much more definite terms the elements of their paradigm, not as a check on &quot;power&quot; (because there is almost no consideration for &quot;balance&quot; between instruments, as your own example displays) but as a method of preserving M20's axis of coincidence.<br /> <br /> In SyndRev, it is possible for a Matter-using syndic's player to, as part of the terms of their effect, state that a given automobile has an untapped hidden feature that improves its gas mileage. This does not require that the player first establish with the ST that the car is of such-and-such a make, and to have a Background to represent their influence in the manufacturer's factories. Rather, the conspiratorial nature of the world exists in an unrealized state, one that resolves into definite effects at player input. M20's concern about PBD seems to mean that it doesn't have such an unrealized state: we have to know if the feature &quot;really exists&quot;<i> - </i>which meansthe conspiracy has to really exist<i> - </i>because PBD won't permit us to elide these steps, any more than it will allow us to &quot;conjure&quot; a cab<i>.</i><br /> <br /> We know that the WoD is haunted by conspiracies as much as it is haunted by the High Ritualist's choirs of angels - but M20 only requires one of these players to buy Backgrounds to make their host of specters &quot;real.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of pointing out something you may have missed but the Technocrat's magic functions on a fundamentally different way than a Traditionalists due to the fact they need foci for everything they do. You actually CAN'T do magic which will allow your car to suddenly have extra-James Bond features. If they weren't built-in ahead of time, you are screwed. That's not how technocratic magic works, they don't do vulgar.<br /> <br /> That's their biggest disadvantage.<br /> <br /> Their big advantage is they are part of the Illuminati and if you want a car equipped with Foci that allows you to be James Bond, all you have to do is fill out a TPS report.<br /> <br /> It takes a lot more effort but basically, if you're a Syndicate mage and you want to spend 40 million dollars without Resources 6, all you need to do is persuade your boss you need the money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T13:56:23-07:00","id":1102350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources?p=1102299#post1102299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It takes a lot more effort but basically, if you're a Syndicate mage and you want to spend 40 million dollars without Resources 6, all you need to do is persuade your boss you need the money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just make $40 million come into existence for whatever purpose you need it and fill out the paperwork to justify it afterwards. Or go golfing with your boss if you don't want to commit anything to a format visible to the NWO. Which doesn't take much effort at all... Probably just some Data and Mind. Maybe some Entropy along with it or after the fact to smooth out any unwanted economic ripples such an Adjustment might cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T15:02:48-07:00","id":1102369,"title":"","content":"Foci does not necessarily mean 'a gadget I built myself.' a Foci is a fairly flexible concept. The NWO are a fairly good example of this. Psychology is their foci for Mind. They talk to you, and things happen. With a convincing argument, a NWO agent, or similarly trained technocrat, can whip a crowd into a frenzy or disburse it. There's no mental thought control laser they have to use. They just use their words. Knowledge can be a focus. Actions can be a focus. A martial arts training camp, is theoretically a focus. Just like the Traditions have their ephemeral foci, so too does the technocracy. In the case of the 'secret car button' the focus is the car. IF there was no car, they couldn't push a secret button on it. If they couldn't push the secret button then no magic would happen.<br /> <br /> And as far as vulgarity goes, several conventions very much so DO use vulgar magic. The difference is, they don't often need to. Why go for the vulgar and flashy plasma cannon if the Thunderhead BFG is just as deadly, and entirely coincidental to the point where it's actually treated as a normal gun unless someone who's not a mage picks it up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T15:50:16-07:00","id":1102389,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone is saying that syndics don't use Instruments or Practices, merely that it does not seem necessary to append additional requirements or costs to certain ones, which M20 does fairly regularly across both the core book and HDYDT. I think &quot;conspiratorial influence&quot; is a perfectly reasonable instrument and that concealed mechanisms are a great vehicle for the &quot;how&quot; of an effect. I don't think this practice/instrument pairing needs to be &quot;justified&quot; by specific Backgrounds, any more than I would require a High Ritualist or Shaman to have Backgrounds stipulating exactly which types of spirits they have pre-existing knowledge of and relationships with. I'm not saying that a Syndic can just wave their hands and teleport, I'm saying I don't think it's necessary to keep track of fictional helicopters that syndics use to rapidly move from place to place, any more than I would require a shaman to keep a roster of (and Contacts dots for) exactly which wind spirits will speed their canoe along.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources?p=1102299#post1102299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You actually CAN'T do magic which will allow your car to suddenly have extra-James Bond features. If they weren't built-in ahead of time, you are screwed. That's not how technocratic magic works, they don't do vulgar.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this instance, I am citing a rote from Syndicate Revised (pg 74), which can indeed create vulgar modifications, though it would typically be coincidental. The mage is not &quot;making it so that the car suddenly has James Bond features&quot;, though. The Rote works by activating features that already &quot;exist.&quot; However, only Enlightened users with adequate clearance and understanding (Read: Matter, Data, or Forces dots, as appropriate) are both aware of these features and have the knowhow to activate them. Sleeper users just can't understand or even <i>discover</i> the hypertech secrets built into their everyday devices.<br /> <br /> These features are created <i>in universe</i> by hypertech engineering and conspiratorial manipulations and have already &quot;existed&quot; (barring wacky readings of the setting metaphysics), but are created <i>for game purposes</i> by the player and storyteller during and as part of the act of making use of the Rote.<br /> <br /> In other words, the feature starts having already always existed when the player rolls Arete.<br /> <br /> This is the unclear narrative space that I was, apparently, failing to describe: The fictional car has no definite features until the ST (and players) work upon it. The act of magic causing the car to activate such a feature also, simultaneously, establishes historical facts about the fictional universe that were previously unclear. Under this Axis of Coincidence, the only &quot;facts&quot; of the car are those established by the people around the table, and coincidental magic can be used to dictate some of these facts - such as heretofore unstated hidden features in a car or building.<br /> <br /> M20's Axis of Coincidence does not allow Matter alone to discover a &quot;hidden feature&quot;, as that is results-based. It doesn't have a &quot;previously unclear&quot; state for the car: the car has implied unstated pre-existing reality that magic must change, evoking each Sphere needed for the procedure in turn. In M20, such an effect would require both Matter for the feature and Mind and Correspondence to compel the engineers to create it and prevent Sleepers from having discovered it; doing so in the field would also potentially require Time to back-project the effect to the object's creation. M20's HR&amp;M sidebar also stipulates that a Syndic intending to do this must have Backgrounds on their character sheet substantiating the influence and connections to the auto industry necessary to have done all this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T06:14:41-07:00","id":1102487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources?p=1101185#post1101185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need Correspondence (and moreover at a level equal to Mind) because you're using the Effect over a distance. If the pilot was present with the helicopter, you wouldn't need to summon it.<br /> <br /> If you were using the helicopter as an Instrument for a Correspondence 3 effect, that's another thing entirely...as well as something with precedent in MtAs. As I said in a previous post, the Order of Reason often used their Enlightened Science to expedite otherwise mundane travel. Infiltrators entered buildings using climbing shoes, lockpicks, and grappling hooks. And explorers would use maps and their knowledge of the environment to make over-land journeys much faster, which often involved taking &quot;shortcuts&quot; that covered more distance than should be realistic. It's entirely possible that modern Technocrats only further refined their methods in this regard.<br /> <br /> No, this isn't exactly teleporting (except when it is). But the Order of Reason book made me consider that Correspondence 3 isn't explicitly about &quot;Teleportation&quot;, but rather &quot;Making intervening space and obstacles not a factor in one's movement&quot;. (Which, really, would also justify using Correspondence 3 to walk through walls. It's not like there's an appreciable practical difference between walking through a wall and teleporting to the other side). But I digress.<br /> <br /> Yes, this is all less efficient than just teleporting. But that deliberate limitation is taken in trade-off for something potentially far more important: being Coincidental. There are ways to make teleportation coincidental, yes, but these ways are not always feasible, nor does a character always believe it can be done (or that the character themselves can do it, even if they believe it theoretically possible). Syndicate reps don't usually study the mind-bending physics needed to fold space, nor can they always afford to rely on gear provided by other Conventions. Nor, again, can they afford to employ such Vulgar methods all the time. For everyday purposes, they are more inclined to leverage their connections, interpersonal skills, and knowledge of geography to call in a helicopter, and then make that helicopter transport them to their location faster than it normally could. An Effect that's completely Coincidental, and which wouldn't cause them to fall from the sky if someone used Countermagic on them (like you said, the helicopter itself is established in the Consensus; the Enlightened Management is just there to make it go faster).<br /> <br /> I find that, when it comes to Paradigm-generated limitations, one must remember that these are features of the Sphere system, not bugs. The Sphere descriptions tell us the upper limit of a mage's capabilities at any given level. It's the Focus - Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments - that tells us how much of that a particular mage can use. Whether &quot;Can Use&quot; is determined by what they believe possible, what they are equipped to pull off, or what they dare do in light of Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources?p=1101680#post1101680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> By contrast, the Syndicate rep just pulls out their cell phone, calls a judge, and makes a deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate member doesn't 'just' do this. The way I understand Syndicate Correspondence (this needs a better name in my opinion) to work:<br /> Syndicate's Correspondence is establishing oneself over the web of business, politics, media, the underworld etc. so that a Syndicate member can indeed act as she was in every situation personally, through phone calls, letters, intermediaries, rumors, SMSes, and video conferences. Her hand is felt everywhere, her name is spoken in hushed whispers, and her influence can close mouths just as readily as it might open them. <i>This</i> is the Correspondence Effect, and it has absolutely nothing to do - both Paradigm-wise and Effect-wise - with a plane or a car going faster, or getting access to the transportation. Transportation being available would be a separate thing - I would say it would be Time 1 Entropy 2-4 to always being able to requisition items from the system(s) at a moment's notice; and in this case it matters not if the Syndicate member would be getting a helicopter or getting the permission to use a large lecturing hall to host a conference.<br /> <br /> If there is no need to leverage presence, reputation and connections in regards to contacting someone, then the Syndic's phone call is not a use of Correspondence 3. (Though it can matter and count in regards to establishing connections and stuff for future Adjustments.) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources?p=1101185#post1101185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said in a previous post, the Order of Reason often used their Enlightened Science to expedite otherwise mundane travel. Infiltrators entered buildings using climbing shoes, lockpicks, and grappling hooks. And explorers would use maps and their knowledge of the environment to make over-land journeys much faster, which often involved taking &quot;shortcuts&quot; that covered more distance than should be realistic. It's entirely possible that modern Technocrats only further refined their methods in this regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those Order of Reason members had appropriate Foci (most of of the time, at least) to account for (or try to explain) how and why this happened. There is no appropriate Foci for a Technocrat as to why a helicopter would go faster except a technological modification. You could say that the pilot is trying his best - but I don't think this is a True Magickal Effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources?p=1101185#post1101185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For everyday purposes, they are more inclined to leverage their connections, interpersonal skills, and knowledge of geography to call in a helicopter...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would the knowledge of geography matter, assuming calling a helicopter is Correspondence 3? All you need is to give your coordinates; there is no True Magick at work here, geography-wise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1100981-management-and-human-resources?p=1102276#post1102276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Syndicate mage uses Spheres and the Instrument-Money, perhaps he is connecting to the underlying hegemony that Syndicate holds over all capitalistic systems. Maybe the Syndicate has a way to co-opt helicopters (or taxis) that are getting ready to go or are ready, but sitting idle. So there's someone who thought they were going to use that helicopter but they just got booted. (Which seems like it makes sense... The helicopter pilot or company gets a deal that can't refuse and boom, here comes your helicopter, Mr. Anderson....)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think and feel this should be Time 1 Entropy 2-4, to represent always being able to get the tools and items you want out of a system(s).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-11-2017, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}